## Model card

- **Name:** Qwen 3.6 Plus
- **Short description:** Alibaba's hosted "Plus" tier of the Qwen3.6 generation — "earlier Qwen multimodal workhorse for million-token agent and document tasks" (models.dev). Released 2026-04-02, ahead of the open Qwen3.6-35B-A3B (Apr 16) and Qwen3.6-27B (Apr 22) releases. Now deprecated on Artificial Analysis in favor of Qwen3.7 Plus.
- **Provider / access:** OpenCode Zen `opencode/qwen-3.6-plus`; Alibaba Cloud Model Studio / DashScope `qwen3.6-plus` (OpenAI- and Anthropic-compatible APIs); 21 third-party providers per models.dev (302.AI, OpenRouter, Vercel AI Gateway, Requesty, Venice, …).
- **Release / knowledge:** Released 2026-04-02 (models.dev + Artificial Analysis FAQ); knowledge cutoff 2025-04 per models.dev.
- **IDs:** `qwen3.6-plus` on DashScope; `opencode/qwen-3.6-plus` on Zen.
- **Context window:** 1,000,000 total; 65,536 max output on standard providers (one gateway lists 250,000) (verified via models.dev + AA; meta.json's "128K total" is a stale placeholder).
- **Modalities:** text + image + video in; text out; reasoning (thinking mode by default, `preserve_thinking` available in the Qwen3.6 generation); tool calls; temperature supported.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-10-01):** first-party $0.50 input / $3.00 output per 1M (90% cache discount, blended $0.43 per 1M per AA); gateway range $0.28–0.33 / $1.65–1.95; bundled free under Alibaba Token Plans (models.dev + AA).
- **Architecture:** proprietary; Alibaba has not disclosed parameter count. Qwen3.6 generation highlights (from the open-model cards): improved agentic coding (frontend workflows, repository-level reasoning) and thinking preservation.

